The source audit caught an important reproducibility nuance: independently asking the provider for 100, 150, … users preserves world seeds and epochs but shifts population-sized RNG draws, so shared users would not have literally identical trajectories. I’m tightening the design to build each world once at the maximum population and take immutable first-\(N\) tape projections. That makes the load axis genuinely nested: every retained user has identical geometry, fading, satellite inventory, seed, and boundary times at every load point.
