The rate-only sweep is now complete for all five targets under both formulations (80 anchor evaluations total). Early evidence is already falsifying a simple “more constraint ⇒ larger gap” story: in the strict margin formulation the pooled gap is +0.110% at 20 Mbit/s, −0.834% at 35, −0.287% at 50, +0.776% at 65, and +0.334% at 80. The sealed formulation is much larger and non-monotone, from +11.041% at 20 to +2.681% at 80. I’m continuing the matched load and joint points; these provisional numbers will be independently replayed before reporting.
